<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title><%= movie.title %></title>
</head>
<body>
  <%# Fields of an object: the same dot notation as in JavaScript %>
  <h1><%= movie.title %> (<%= movie.year %>)</h1>
  <p><%= movie.rated %> · <%= movie.runtime %> min · <%= movie.genres.join(', ') %></p>
  <p><%= movie.plot %></p>

  <%# A decision: the scriptlet tag runs the if, and prints nothing itself %>
  <% if (movie.imdb.rating >= 8) { %>
    <p><strong>Must watch</strong> - IMDb <%= movie.imdb.rating %></p>
  <% } else { %>
    <p>IMDb <%= movie.imdb.rating %></p>
  <% } %>

  <h2>A review someone typed</h2>
  <h3>Escaped: &lt;%= review %&gt;</h3>
  <p><%= review %></p>

  <h3>Raw: &lt;%- review %&gt;</h3>
  <p><%- review %></p>
  <p>The escaped one shows the tags as text. The raw one ran them - including the script.</p>
</body>
</html>
